From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Picture Password as a quick second unlock

Plan phase D, after BlackBerry 10's Picture Password: over the user's
photo, move a grid of digits until the secret digit sits on the secret
spot. It is a second, quicker unlock: the PIN or password stays the
device credential and still decrypts storage.

* Bouncer: KeyguardAbsKeyInputViewController shows it over the PIN or
  password bouncer when it is set up, the platform allows a quick unlock
  (KeyguardUpdateMonitor.isUnlockingWithBiometricAllowed(true): false
  after a reboot and after the 72-hour strong-auth timeout, the rules
  fingerprint follows; the Q25 has no fingerprint reader) and fewer than
  5 pictures were wrong. Esc returns to the PIN. A match dismisses the
  keyguard for that user; a PIN or password unlock clears the count.
* Trackpad first: arrows (or a drag) move the grid one cell with a
  tick, Enter submits; typing never enters the number, and the view is
  hidden from accessibility so a screen reader cannot speak the digits.
* No smudge trail: each round starts at a random offset with the digits
  in a fresh random order.
* Optional second number, "Stronger" (owner decision 2026-11-05: a
  setup option, off by default): a second, reshuffled round; a mistake
  is reported only after the last round, never which one.
* Precision: the exact spot, or one cell either way (shown as weaker);
  grid 8 to 12 cells a side.
* Setup: SablePicturePasswordSetupActivity
  (org.sableos.keyguard.action.PICTURE_PASSWORD, from Settings > Sable)
  confirms the PIN or password first, then photo, grid, precision,
  Stronger, each digit (typed) and spot (trackpad), and 3 practice
  unlocks before saving. Owner only.
* Storage: SystemUI's credential-encrypted storage, readable only after
  the first PIN unlock; each number as a salted, iterated SHA-256 of
  digit and spot. With at most 1,440 choices per number that cannot
  resist an offline search, so the protection is the storage and the
  5-try limit, as on BlackBerry 10.

Pure policy: keyguard/sable/SablePicturePassword.java.
